{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Moses took of the anointing oil, and of the blood which was upon the altar</b>. I do not know whether he mixed them together for this sprinkling, as in \"And he shall take of the blood of the bull and of the blood of the goat, and put it upon the horns of the altar\" (Leviticus 16:18). Likewise, the reason for delaying these sprinklings until after the burning-up of the ordination offering is not clear to me, for in the command (Exodus 29:21) he gave the sprinklings first and afterward said, \"And you shall take of the ram — the fat, and the rump\" (ibid. v. 22). Perhaps it is because it says there (Leviticus 8:21), \"And it is holy, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons' garments with him,\" Moses learned that this is the final act performed upon them, through which they would become consecrated completely — for there, in the anointing (ibid. v. 7), he did not mention consecration, nor in the putting of blood on the extremities (ibid. v. 20) — whereas here it says, \"And he anointed him, to consecrate him\" (Leviticus 8:12), not that he was consecrated completely, until he performed these sprinklings and said of them (here), \"And he consecrated Aaron and his sons.\" And so he completed the consecration of the father and the sons together by means of these sprinklings. And thus they said in Sifra (Tzav, Milu'im 34): \"And he consecrated Aaron\" — from this you learn that the consecration of Aaron and his sons was not completed except by the sprinkling of blood."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:51.741677190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}